This is to build sdcard image for rpi4b, rpi5, opi5+, rockpi4b and roc-rk3328-cc.

Parts needed:
1. Raspberry pi 4b, Raspberry pi 5, orangepi5plus, rockpi4b and roc-rk3328-cc.
2. WD Black SN770 1TB NVMe SSD.
3. Sandisk 64GB micro sdcard.
4. usb3 stick.
5. Host PC with fedora 44.
6. ASUS USB-BT500 bluetooth usb dongle.

Steps to build rpi4b, rpi5, opi5+, rockpi4b, roc-rk3328-cc sdcard image:

1. git clone https://github.com/philipchen888/build-5sbc.git
   sudo dnf update
   sudo dnf install debootstrap qemu-user-static gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu bison flex elfutils-libelf-devel openssl-devel tar chrpath diffstat rpcgen python3-setuptools swig python3-devel openssl-devel-engine gnutls-devel python3-pyelftools gcc-c++ cmake libfdt-devel git bc ncurses-devel gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu binutils-aarch64-linux-gnu adb rkdeveloptool android-tools libusb1 libusb1-devel

   cd ~/Downloads
   wget https://github.com/pftf/RPi4/releases/download/v1.53/RPi4_UEFI_Firmware_v1.53.zip
   mv RPi4_UEFI_Firmware_v1.53.zip RPi4_UEFI_Firmware.zip
   wget https://github.com/worproject/rpi5-uefi/releases/download/v0.3/RPi5_UEFI_Release_v0.3.zip
   mv RPi5_UEFI_Release_v0.3.zip RPi5_UEFI_Release.zip

2. cd ~/build-5sbc/uboot  ( Download u-boot to spi for rockchip )
   Program spi flash with RK3588_NOR_FLASH.img for uefi boot:
   Build RK3588_NOR_FLASH.img from git clone https://github.com/edk2-porting/edk2-rk3588.git --recursive
   cd edk2-rk3588; ./build.sh --device orangepi-5plus --release Release
   The result is in ~/build-rockchip/uboot/edk2-rk3588/RK3588_NOR_FLASH.img

   Prepare spi nor flash for extlinux boot:
   Download u-boot-v2024.07-orangepi5-plus-spi.bin
   Erase spi flash
   Program spi flash with u-boot-v2024.07-orangepi5-plus-spi.bin
   Boot NVMe without sdcard.

3. cd ~/build-5sbc/kernel ( Compile vendor's kernel for rpi, compile mainline kernel for rockchip )
   git clone https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux --depth=1 -b rpi-7.2.y
   For rpi4b:
   vi ./linux/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig ( delete CONFIG_CMDLINE, change CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=m to CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=y )
   Use ovmerge to change bcm2711-rpi-4-b.dts to include some dtoverlay ( uart2, vc4, i2c, spi etc.).
   make MYCHIP=bcm2711 kernel

   For rpi5:
   vi ./linux/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2712_defconfig ( delete CONFIG_CMDLINE, change CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=m to CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=y )
   Use ovmerge to change bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dts to include some dtoverlay ( uart2, vc4, i2c, spi etc.).
   make MYCHIP=bcm2712 kernel

4. cd ~/build-5sbc/debian         ( Build debian bookworm, trixie, forky images )

5. cd ~/build-5sbc/ubuntu         ( Build ubuntu noble, questing, resolute images )

6. cd ~/build-5sbc/fedora         ( Build fedora image )

7. cd ~/build-5sbc/flightaware    ( Build flightaware )

8. cd ~/build-5sbc/yocto          ( Build yocto image )

9. cd ~/build-5sbc/buildroot      ( Build buildroot image )

10. cd ~/build-5sbc/android       ( Build android image )
